What Is the Lithium Carbonate Market?
Lithium carbonate is a refined lithium chemical used primarily in rechargeable battery cathode manufacturing, as well as selected pharmaceutical and specialty chemical applications. It is produced through the processing of lithium-bearing brines or minerals, followed by concentration, purification, and chemical conversion.

Battery-grade lithium carbonate is particularly important for cathode materials used in lithium-ion batteries, including lithium iron phosphate chemistry. Product quality depends on purity, impurity control, consistency, and reliable supply to downstream manufacturers.

